# One ID per line, reason and expiry above it (CLAUDE.md "Security scanning with Trivy").
#
# AWS-0104: egress to 0.0.0.0/0 in infra/aws/main.tf, limited to ports 443, 80, 6379, 53/udp,
# 123/udp (plus 5432 on the control host). Upstash, Neon and S3 have no fixed IP ranges and
# there is no NAT or VPC endpoint by design (cost rule), so the destination cannot be narrowed.
# The sandbox itself has no network. Revisit in Phase 13; expires 2027-01-03.
AWS-0104 exp:2027-01-03
#
# AWS-0132: the data bucket (infra/bootstrap/main.tf) uses SSE-S3 (AES256), not a customer managed KMS key.
# The bucket holds problem bundles and tfstate, no user data. A CMK adds a recurring KMS cost
# (about 1 USD per month per key plus requests) for key-rotation control we do not need yet.
# Owner decision recorded in docs/security-review.md (SEC-12). Expires 2027-04-03.
AWS-0132 exp:2027-04-03
